(Reading in a foreign language is an exercise in patience. The eye) Tj
T*
(moves quickly, the mind lags behind, and an unfamiliar word can halt) Tj
T*
(the whole sentence. A dictionary that interrupts this rhythm costs) Tj
T*
(more than it gives.) Tj
T*
T*
(The best tools of this kind are almost invisible. They wait at the) Tj
T*
(edge of your attention, offer a definition when curiosity appears, and) Tj
T*
(then disappear. Nothing is copied, nothing is saved, and nothing is) Tj
T*
(uploaded; the reader simply keeps reading.) Tj
T*
T*
(Consider the word deliberate. Seen once, it is a small puzzle; seen) Tj
T*
(three times, in three different sentences, it becomes part of your) Tj
T*
(vocabulary. That slow accumulation is the whole point of practice.) Tj
